  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support for Agricultural Production and Food Security For Vulnerable Families in the Cotes de Fer District in South-East Hati</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OPLA will organize project activities with three local farmer organizations. It will train their members and farmers on agroecological practices that will improve production increase revenue and ensure sustainable access to food supplies. OPLA will work with farmers to establish a grain mill two veterinary centers and home gardens and form or strengthen savings and loan organizations. The project will benefit about 1500 farmers directly and another 6000 indirectly in the Ctes-de-Fer district in Haiti&apos;s Sud-Est department.</narrative>
  </description>
